# tally 2.2.1 R20 (L §6.1 l.1802, OPERATIONS §2.1): a member's ask brings to the run's own level its refused scenario's
# line, its own when refused alone and its walk's warnings, never WARN-UNREAD, by the joint model's names, once per member;
# the lines under its result are the member's.
# C-13 on the critic's jw: two members of one text whose walks warn alike: two last lines, a.konto and b.konto.
# tally 2.2 printed none for a.q, b.q.
=== a/a.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source plan "p"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

kind rents: event certain
  leg cash: PLN

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..

place spare: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..2026-06-30

place landlord: outside lives 1900-01-01..

input rent_amt: money PLN

input back_amt: money PLN

input act_day: date

input back_day: date

input zero: int

input one_amt: money PLN

input gap_day: date

input d_open: date

move rent[m in months]: rents
  on start_of(m)
  at start_of(m)
  leg cash from konto to landlord amount rent_amt

move back[a in adjustments over .. where a.adjusts in rents and act_day < back_day]: transfers
  on act_day
  at a.day
  leg cash from konto to landlord amount back_amt
  fulfils a

version v
  cite plan
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  rent_amt = 900.00 PLN
  back_amt = 100.00 PLN

version v2
  cite plan
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-03-15
  replace rent_amt = 950.00 PLN "raise"

version day
  cite plan
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  act_day = 2026-04-05
  back_day = 2026-04-20

version fixed
  cite plan
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  zero = 0
  one_amt = 1.00 PLN
  d_open = 2026-01-01
  opening[spare] = 100.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "w"

ask q: bal(konto, 2026-04-30) law cut
=== a/asks.tally
part asks
  tally 2

ask q_u: unit(konto) == PLN, unit(bal(konto, 2026-04-30))
ask q_n: count(x in places over .. where x in accounts and unit(x) == PLN)
ask q_base_gone: bal(konto, 2026-04-30) in nowhere2 law cut
ask warning_x: bal(spare, 2026-01-31) law cut
=== a/sc.tally
scenario sc over m
  tally 2
  from 2026-03-01

version day2
  cite plan
  governs 2026-03-01..
  known 2026-01-01
  replace act_day = 2026-04-25

ask q_sc: bal(konto, 2026-04-30) in sc law cut
ask q_d: diff(bal(konto, 2026-04-30)) in sc against m law cut
ask q_late: bal(konto, 2026-04-30) in sc law cut as known 2026-07-01
ask q_gone: bal(konto, 2026-04-30) in nowhere law cut
